1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,015
Almost four hundred years ago,

2
00:00:02,015 --> 00:00:06,635
a scientist called Jan van Helmont
planted a small willow tree in a pot of

3
00:00:06,635 --> 00:00:07,704
dry soil.

4
00:00:07,704 --> 00:00:09,436
He weighed the tree.

5
00:00:09,436 --> 00:00:11,168
He weighed the soil.

6
00:00:11,168 --> 00:00:12,880
Then, for five years,

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:16,958
he gave it nothing but
water. The tree grew.

8
00:00:16,958 --> 00:00:20,939
It gained about seventy-four
kilograms. And the soil?

9
00:00:20,939 --> 00:00:23,622
It had lost about fifty-seven grams.

10
00:00:24,022 --> 00:00:29,352
So where did a whole tree's worth
of mass come from? Not the soil.

11
00:00:29,352 --> 00:00:32,040
Most of it came out of thin air.

12
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:38,713
You eat to get your
food. Plants don't.

13
00:00:38,713 --> 00:00:41,977
They make their own,
by photosynthesis.

14
00:00:41,977 --> 00:00:45,009
Here's the definition
the mark scheme wants.

15
00:00:45,009 --> 00:00:49,003
Photosynthesis is the process by
which plants synthesise carbohydrates

16
00:00:49,003 --> 00:00:52,135
from raw materials
using energy from light.

17
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:54,496
Synthesise just means make.

18
00:00:54,496 --> 00:00:58,337
The carbohydrate they make
first is glucose, a sugar.

19
00:00:58,337 --> 00:01:01,630
The raw materials are
carbon dioxide and water.

20
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:04,172
And the energy comes from light.

21
00:01:04,522 --> 00:01:06,442
Here's the word equation.

22
00:01:06,442 --> 00:01:08,436
Carbon dioxide, plus water,

23
00:01:08,436 --> 00:01:10,690
gives glucose, plus oxygen.

24
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,860
Light and chlorophyll go above
the arrow. They're conditions,

25
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:16,464
not reactants.

26
00:01:16,464 --> 00:01:20,279
The carbon dioxide diffuses
into the leaf from the air.

27
00:01:20,279 --> 00:01:22,367
The water comes from the soil,

28
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:25,023
up through the roots and the xylem.

29
00:01:25,023 --> 00:01:27,371
The oxygen is a waste product.

30
00:01:27,371 --> 00:01:29,292
Some is used in respiration,

31
00:01:29,292 --> 00:01:32,262
and the rest diffuses
out of the leaf.

32
00:01:32,562 --> 00:01:34,175
For the Extended paper,

33
00:01:34,175 --> 00:01:36,544
learn the balanced equation too.

34
00:01:36,544 --> 00:01:39,736
Six C O two, plus six H two O,

35
00:01:39,736 --> 00:01:42,275
gives C six H twelve O six,

36
00:01:42,275 --> 00:01:43,945
plus six O two.

37
00:01:43,945 --> 00:01:48,376
Six carbons, twelve hydrogens and
eighteen oxygens on each side.

38
00:01:48,376 --> 00:01:49,686
It balances.

39
00:01:50,036 --> 00:01:52,892
So what does the light actually do?

40
00:01:52,892 --> 00:01:55,710
Inside the leaf's
cells are chloroplasts.

41
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:58,815
They contain chlorophyll,
a green pigment.

42
00:01:58,815 --> 00:02:00,496
Chlorophyll absorbs light,

43
00:02:00,496 --> 00:02:04,152
and transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals:

44
00:02:04,152 --> 00:02:07,176
the chemical energy
stored in glucose.

45
00:02:07,176 --> 00:02:09,498
Careful with your wording here.

46
00:02:09,498 --> 00:02:11,747
Chlorophyll doesn't make energy.

47
00:02:11,747 --> 00:02:14,950
Energy can't be made.
It transfers it.

48
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:17,953
So use the syllabus word: transfers.

49
00:02:18,303 --> 00:02:20,651
So the plant has made glucose.

50
00:02:20,651 --> 00:02:23,017
What does it do with it?

51
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,742
Some is used straight
away in respiration,

52
00:02:25,742 --> 00:02:27,307
to release energy.

53
00:02:27,307 --> 00:02:29,181
Some is turned into starch,

54
00:02:29,181 --> 00:02:30,866
as an energy store.

55
00:02:30,866 --> 00:02:32,265
Starch is insoluble,

56
00:02:32,265 --> 00:02:35,276
so it doesn't affect
osmosis in the cells.

57
00:02:35,276 --> 00:02:36,816
Some becomes cellulose,

58
00:02:36,816 --> 00:02:38,548
to build cell walls.

59
00:02:38,548 --> 00:02:40,516
Some is changed into sucrose,

60
00:02:40,516 --> 00:02:44,451
for transport in the phloem
to other parts of the plant.

61
00:02:44,451 --> 00:02:46,774
And some becomes nectar in flowers,

62
00:02:46,774 --> 00:02:49,584
to attract insects for pollination.

63
00:02:49,584 --> 00:02:51,103
Respiration, starch,

64
00:02:51,103 --> 00:02:52,575
cellulose, sucrose,

65
00:02:52,575 --> 00:02:55,001
nectar. Learn all five.

66
00:02:55,351 --> 00:02:57,246
Glucose only contains carbon,

67
00:02:57,246 --> 00:02:58,905
hydrogen and oxygen.

68
00:02:58,905 --> 00:03:01,849
But to grow, a plant
also needs proteins,

69
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:04,291
which are made from amino acids.

70
00:03:04,291 --> 00:03:06,707
And amino acids contain nitrogen.

71
00:03:06,707 --> 00:03:09,599
So plants absorb nitrate
ions from the soil,

72
00:03:09,599 --> 00:03:11,258
through their roots.

73
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:14,410
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

74
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:16,806
Without enough, growth is stunted,

75
00:03:16,806 --> 00:03:19,595
and the older leaves turn yellow.

76
00:03:19,595 --> 00:03:22,768
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

77
00:03:22,768 --> 00:03:26,537
Without enough, the leaves
turn yellow between the veins,

78
00:03:26,537 --> 00:03:28,364
so less light is absorbed,

79
00:03:28,364 --> 00:03:30,713
and there's less photosynthesis.

80
00:03:31,063 --> 00:03:33,975
Most photosynthesis
happens in the leaves.

81
00:03:33,975 --> 00:03:36,631
And most leaves are broad and thin.

82
00:03:36,631 --> 00:03:38,860
Broad gives a large surface area,

83
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,639
to absorb more light.

84
00:03:40,639 --> 00:03:44,925
Thin means a short distance for carbon
dioxide to diffuse to the cells

85
00:03:44,925 --> 00:03:45,927
inside.

86
00:03:46,227 --> 00:03:47,865
Let's cut one open.

87
00:03:47,865 --> 00:03:51,775
This is a cross-section of a leaf
from a dicotyledonous plant,

88
00:03:51,775 --> 00:03:53,058
like a bean.

89
00:03:53,058 --> 00:03:54,765
It's a simplified diagram,

90
00:03:54,765 --> 00:03:57,125
so let's go layer by layer.

91
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:59,358
On top, the waxy cuticle.

92
00:03:59,358 --> 00:04:00,924
It reduces water loss,

93
00:04:00,924 --> 00:04:02,323
and it's transparent,

94
00:04:02,323 --> 00:04:04,739
so light passes straight through.

95
00:04:04,739 --> 00:04:07,207
Under it, the upper epidermis.

96
00:04:07,207 --> 00:04:09,222
Its cells are transparent too,

97
00:04:09,222 --> 00:04:10,668
with no chloroplasts,

98
00:04:10,668 --> 00:04:13,157
so light reaches the layer below.

99
00:04:13,157 --> 00:04:14,957
The palisade mesophyll.

100
00:04:14,957 --> 00:04:17,781
Tall cells, tightly
packed near the top,

101
00:04:17,781 --> 00:04:19,748
and full of chloroplasts.

102
00:04:19,748 --> 00:04:21,622
They absorb the most light,

103
00:04:21,622 --> 00:04:24,848
so this is where most
photosynthesis happens.

104
00:04:25,198 --> 00:04:27,807
Below that, the spongy mesophyll.

105
00:04:27,807 --> 00:04:29,942
Rounder cells, loosely packed,

106
00:04:29,942 --> 00:04:32,170
with air spaces between them.

107
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:35,725
The air spaces let carbon
dioxide diffuse to the cells,

108
00:04:35,725 --> 00:04:39,391
and give a large surface
area for gas exchange.

109
00:04:39,391 --> 00:04:42,564
Running through the leaf
are vascular bundles.

110
00:04:42,564 --> 00:04:45,408
Xylem brings in water
and mineral ions.

111
00:04:45,408 --> 00:04:48,227
Phloem carries sucrose
and amino acids away,

112
00:04:48,227 --> 00:04:50,640
to the rest of the plant.

113
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:53,297
On the underside,
the lower epidermis,

114
00:04:53,297 --> 00:04:55,619
with tiny pores called stomata.

115
00:04:55,619 --> 00:04:58,177
Carbon dioxide diffuses
in through them,

116
00:04:58,177 --> 00:05:00,097
and oxygen diffuses out.

117
00:05:00,097 --> 00:05:04,252
Each stoma is opened and closed
by a pair of guard cells.

118
00:05:04,602 --> 00:05:08,370
So how do you prove a leaf
has been photosynthesising?

119
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:10,355
Test it for starch.

120
00:05:10,355 --> 00:05:12,562
First, destarch the plant.

121
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:15,318
Leave it in the dark
for a day or two,

122
00:05:15,318 --> 00:05:17,833
so it uses up its stored starch.

123
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:23,060
Then any starch you find later must
have been made during your experiment.

124
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:23,949
Step one:

125
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,297
put the leaf in boiling water.

126
00:05:26,297 --> 00:05:30,896
This kills it, and breaks down the
cell membranes so the iodine can get

127
00:05:30,896 --> 00:05:32,499
in. Step two:

128
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,373
turn off the Bunsen burner,

129
00:05:34,373 --> 00:05:36,628
and put the leaf in hot ethanol,

130
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:38,172
in a water bath.

131
00:05:38,172 --> 00:05:39,618
Ethanol is flammable,

132
00:05:39,618 --> 00:05:41,256
so no naked flame.

133
00:05:41,256 --> 00:05:43,553
The ethanol removes the chlorophyll,

134
00:05:43,553 --> 00:05:47,098
so you can see the colour
change. Step three:

135
00:05:47,098 --> 00:05:50,716
dip it in warm water to
soften it. Step four:

136
00:05:50,716 --> 00:05:52,616
spread it on a white tile,

137
00:05:52,616 --> 00:05:54,536
and add iodine solution.

138
00:05:54,536 --> 00:05:56,999
Blue-black means starch is present.

139
00:05:56,999 --> 00:05:59,207
Orange-brown means no starch.

140
00:05:59,557 --> 00:06:03,158
Now use that test to show
what photosynthesis needs.

141
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:05,347
Each experiment needs a control:

142
00:06:05,347 --> 00:06:09,321
identical, except for the
one factor you're testing.

143
00:06:09,321 --> 00:06:11,844
Chlorophyll: use a variegated leaf,

144
00:06:11,844 --> 00:06:14,735
one that's partly
green and partly white.

145
00:06:14,735 --> 00:06:17,105
The white parts have no chlorophyll,

146
00:06:17,105 --> 00:06:18,483
so after the test,

147
00:06:18,483 --> 00:06:21,413
only the green parts turn blue-black.

148
00:06:21,413 --> 00:06:24,698
Light: cover part of a
leaf with black paper,

149
00:06:24,698 --> 00:06:28,304
and leave the plant in
the light for a few hours.

150
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:30,981
Only the uncovered part makes starch.

151
00:06:30,981 --> 00:06:34,988
The uncovered part is the
control. Carbon dioxide:

152
00:06:34,988 --> 00:06:37,671
seal a leaf in a
flask with soda lime,

153
00:06:37,671 --> 00:06:39,826
which absorbs carbon dioxide.

154
00:06:39,826 --> 00:06:43,500
The control is an identical
flask with no soda lime.

155
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:46,524
Only the control leaf
turns blue-black.

156
00:06:46,524 --> 00:06:48,748
So photosynthesis needs chlorophyll,

157
00:06:48,748 --> 00:06:51,055
light, and carbon dioxide.

158
00:06:51,405 --> 00:06:55,126
To measure the rate of
photosynthesis, use pondweed.

159
00:06:55,126 --> 00:06:58,608
Put it in water with a little
sodium hydrogencarbonate,

160
00:06:58,608 --> 00:07:00,810
which supplies carbon dioxide.

161
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:04,275
In the light, it gives
off bubbles of oxygen.

162
00:07:04,275 --> 00:07:06,503
Count the bubbles per minute.

163
00:07:06,503 --> 00:07:08,711
Or, for more accurate results,

164
00:07:08,711 --> 00:07:11,295
collect the gas and
measure its volume,

165
00:07:11,295 --> 00:07:13,823
because bubbles vary in size.

166
00:07:13,823 --> 00:07:15,838
To change the light intensity,

167
00:07:15,838 --> 00:07:18,494
move a lamp closer or further away.

168
00:07:18,494 --> 00:07:20,516
Keep everything else constant:

169
00:07:20,516 --> 00:07:24,071
the same plant, the same
carbon dioxide concentration,

170
00:07:24,071 --> 00:07:26,038
and the same temperature.

171
00:07:26,038 --> 00:07:27,416
An LED lamp helps,

172
00:07:27,416 --> 00:07:30,513
because it gives off
very little heat.

173
00:07:30,513 --> 00:07:32,408
As light intensity increases,

174
00:07:32,408 --> 00:07:35,231
the rate increases, then levels off.

175
00:07:35,231 --> 00:07:37,810
Increase the carbon
dioxide concentration,

176
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:39,837
and you get the same shape:

177
00:07:39,837 --> 00:07:41,976
a rise, then a plateau.

178
00:07:41,976 --> 00:07:43,870
Temperature is different.

179
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:45,911
The rate rises to an optimum,

180
00:07:45,911 --> 00:07:47,523
then falls quickly.

181
00:07:47,523 --> 00:07:51,286
The reactions of photosynthesis
are catalysed by enzymes.

182
00:07:51,286 --> 00:07:52,591
Below the optimum,

183
00:07:52,591 --> 00:07:54,961
more heat means more kinetic energy,

184
00:07:54,961 --> 00:07:56,620
and more collisions.

185
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:59,543
Above it, the enzymes are denatured.

186
00:07:59,893 --> 00:08:02,415
Extended now: limiting factors.

187
00:08:02,415 --> 00:08:07,428
A limiting factor is something in
short supply that restricts the rate.

188
00:08:07,428 --> 00:08:09,776
Look at the light graph again.

189
00:08:09,776 --> 00:08:12,955
Here, the rate rises as
light intensity rises,

190
00:08:12,955 --> 00:08:15,940
so light intensity is
the limiting factor.

191
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:18,810
Here, more light makes no difference.

192
00:08:18,810 --> 00:08:20,991
Light is no longer limiting.

193
00:08:20,991 --> 00:08:22,296
Something else is,

194
00:08:22,296 --> 00:08:25,777
like carbon dioxide
concentration, or temperature.

195
00:08:25,777 --> 00:08:27,484
Raise the carbon dioxide,

196
00:08:27,484 --> 00:08:29,926
and the curve levels off higher.

197
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,997
That shows carbon
dioxide was limiting.

198
00:08:32,997 --> 00:08:35,727
In the exam, name
the limiting factor,

199
00:08:35,727 --> 00:08:37,279
and give the reason:

200
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:39,995
increasing it increases the rate.

201
00:08:39,995 --> 00:08:42,813
Different conditions,
different limits.

202
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:44,979
At dawn, or on a dull day,

203
00:08:44,979 --> 00:08:46,544
it's usually light.

204
00:08:46,544 --> 00:08:48,183
On a cold winter's day,

205
00:08:48,183 --> 00:08:49,936
it's often temperature.

206
00:08:49,936 --> 00:08:52,217
On a bright, warm summer's day,

207
00:08:52,217 --> 00:08:54,284
it's often carbon dioxide.

208
00:08:54,634 --> 00:08:55,986
One more practical,

209
00:08:55,986 --> 00:08:57,859
for the Extended paper.

210
00:08:57,859 --> 00:09:01,691
Hydrogencarbonate indicator shows
how much carbon dioxide is in a

211
00:09:01,691 --> 00:09:05,228
solution. At normal
air levels, it's red.

212
00:09:05,228 --> 00:09:06,627
More carbon dioxide,

213
00:09:06,627 --> 00:09:08,359
and it turns yellow.

214
00:09:08,359 --> 00:09:09,758
Less carbon dioxide,

215
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:11,790
and it turns purple.

216
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:13,757
Three tubes of indicator.

217
00:09:13,757 --> 00:09:16,512
One with a leaf, in bright light.

218
00:09:16,512 --> 00:09:20,290
One with a leaf, wrapped
in foil, so it's dark.

219
00:09:20,290 --> 00:09:22,617
And one with no leaf at all.

220
00:09:22,617 --> 00:09:24,705
What colour will each tube be,

221
00:09:24,705 --> 00:09:26,443
after a few hours?

222
00:09:26,943 --> 00:09:30,221
Pause the video, and
make your prediction.

223
00:09:34,571 --> 00:09:36,183
Here's what happens.

224
00:09:36,183 --> 00:09:39,314
In the light, the
indicator turns purple.

225
00:09:39,314 --> 00:09:41,893
Photosynthesis is faster
than respiration,

226
00:09:41,893 --> 00:09:46,042
so the leaf takes in more carbon
dioxide than it gives out.

227
00:09:46,042 --> 00:09:48,536
In the dark, it turns yellow.

228
00:09:48,536 --> 00:09:50,170
There's no photosynthesis,

229
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:51,971
but respiration carries on,

230
00:09:51,971 --> 00:09:54,246
so carbon dioxide is released.

231
00:09:54,246 --> 00:09:58,052
The tube with no leaf stays
red. It's the control:

232
00:09:58,052 --> 00:10:00,802
it shows the leaf caused the changes.

233
00:10:00,802 --> 00:10:03,960
And in dim light, the
two rates can balance,

234
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:06,194
so the indicator stays red.

235
00:10:06,494 --> 00:10:08,448
Which busts a classic myth:

236
00:10:08,448 --> 00:10:11,689
that plants photosynthesise
instead of respiring.

237
00:10:11,689 --> 00:10:13,610
Plants respire all the time,

238
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:16,104
day and night, just like you.

239
00:10:16,104 --> 00:10:19,257
In bright light,
photosynthesis is just faster,

240
00:10:19,257 --> 00:10:22,268
so there's a net uptake
of carbon dioxide.

241
00:10:22,268 --> 00:10:25,024
Net is the word examiners look for.

242
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:28,009
So, back to van Helmont's willow.

243
00:10:28,009 --> 00:10:31,221
Where did seventy-four
kilograms come from?

244
00:10:31,221 --> 00:10:33,382
Carbon dioxide, from the air,

245
00:10:33,382 --> 00:10:35,615
and water, from the soil.

246
00:10:35,615 --> 00:10:36,967
Built into glucose,

247
00:10:36,967 --> 00:10:38,366
then into cellulose,

248
00:10:38,366 --> 00:10:40,025
starch and proteins.

249
00:10:40,025 --> 00:10:43,606
The soil itself gave only a
few grams of mineral ions,

250
00:10:43,606 --> 00:10:45,967
like nitrate and magnesium.

251
00:10:45,967 --> 00:10:49,333
Van Helmont thought his
tree was made of water.

252
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:51,379
He was only half right.

253
00:10:51,679 --> 00:10:54,148
The rest was built out of thin air,

254
00:10:54,148 --> 00:10:56,168
using energy from light.

255
00:10:56,518 --> 00:10:57,728
Quick recap.

256
00:10:57,728 --> 00:11:00,996
Carbon dioxide plus water
gives glucose plus oxygen,

257
00:11:00,996 --> 00:11:02,916
using energy from light.

258
00:11:02,916 --> 00:11:05,306
Chlorophyll transfers that energy.

259
00:11:05,306 --> 00:11:07,368
Glucose is used in respiration,

260
00:11:07,368 --> 00:11:08,673
or becomes starch,

261
00:11:08,673 --> 00:11:11,021
cellulose, sucrose or nectar.

262
00:11:11,021 --> 00:11:12,941
Nitrate for amino acids.

263
00:11:12,941 --> 00:11:14,882
Magnesium for chlorophyll.

264
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,688
Leaves are broad, thin,

265
00:11:16,688 --> 00:11:18,420
and built in layers.

